---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { siteName } from '../lib/site';
---

<Layout
	title={`Scoring | ${siteName}`}
	description={`Each ${siteName} listing is scored out of 10 for real autonomy, reliability, usefulness, pricing value, and current limitations.`}
>
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
		<p class="section-kicker">Scoring</p>
		<h1 class="mt-2 font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-[2.6rem]">
			How we score agents
		</h1>
		<div class="prose prose-lg prose-agenthub mt-8 dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
			<p>Each agent is scored out of 10 based on:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Real autonomy (can it do work without constant prompting?)</li>
				<li>Reliability and production hours, not launch clips</li>
				<li>Usefulness for practical tasks</li>
				<li>Pricing value and whether you can actually buy it</li>
				<li>Current limitations</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				A high score does not mean perfect. It means the product is meaningfully capable today.
				9 and above is almost empty on purpose. An 8 needs boring production hours.
			</p>
			<p>
				A Grok Bot template — or any other packaged prompt, skill, or role card — is not a listing.
				The platform that takes action is.
			</p>
			<p>Scores are editorial, not a bake-off. We update them when the product changes.</p>
		</div>
		<p class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
			<a href="/agents" class="btn-primary">Browse scored agents <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
			<a href="/about" class="btn-ghost">About {siteName}</a>
		</p>
	</section>
</Layout>
